(*
env: OEVM_OTA_TRIAL=1
expect:
trial true
the record is stageable 32
pending before 0
pending after 0
still here — otaCheck returned and nothing exited
*)
(* rete#25 — A TRIAL-UNCONFIRMED NODE MUST NOT STAGE. The finding came out of the
   Task 8 runner review; the fix is node-side, so the test is here.

   The chain being closed: a trial node that stages exits 42, and the runner
   handles exit-42 BEFORE the trial-unconfirmed revert (design §5 step 3, in that
   written order), so the manifest ends with `active` = an image that was never
   confirmed and `prev` cleared to the image that was itself on trial. The last
   known-good image is then in neither slot. Reordering the runner is worse: by
   exit-42 the staging has already overwritten the rollback slot, so a
   revert-first runner verify-fails against a cleared `prev` and exits 3 — a
   brick rather than a bad manifest. So the node simply does not start a stage it
   cannot afford to finish.

   `OEVM_OTA_TRIAL=1` is per-test (tuvm#88): exported globally it would leak into
   24_ota/01, which asserts `trial false`.

   WHY THIS IS TESTABLE WITHOUT A NETWORK. `otaCheck` is one decision, and every
   step before the stage is local: the confirm needs `acked > 0`, which a bridge
   that has never exchanged does not have; the goal is a cell this test plants
   itself; and `otaIsRunning:` is false because no `OEVM_IMAGE_HASH` is set. The
   step that would reach the block plane is `otaStage:`, and it is exactly the
   step the guard must prevent. With the guard deleted this file prints
   `pending after 1` and the C seam's own `ota: no staging slot (OEVM_OTA_STAGE
   unset)` — measured, not assumed. Note what that means: the seam refuses before
   any I/O, so the regression is caught by the LOG ENTRY and not by a timeout,
   which is why `pending` is asserted rather than elapsed time.

   THE FALSIFIER IS THE SECOND LINE. A test that planted a malformed record, or
   one whose hash happened to match, would pass for the wrong reason and would
   keep passing after the guard was deleted. So the record is handed to
   `otaWantedFrom:` first and asserted STAGEABLE — 32 bytes of hash come back —
   before `otaCheck` is asked to ignore it. Without that line the whole file is
   theatre.

   `pending` is the assertion surface because `tel/log` is a stream: the bridge's
   own capture reaction is the only thing that retains an entry, so a subscribed
   bridge with an empty pending queue after a drain is the same claim as "no log
   line was written", and it needs no gateway. Both `ota staged` and
   `ota stage failed` would land there, so the guard is distinguished from a
   stage that merely failed. *)
class TrialDefersStage packageUsing: manifest = () (
  public main: platform args: args = (
    | space bridge rec |
    space:: platform space.
    bridge:: platform PortaBridge socket: nil space: space id: 'n1'
               peer: '::1' port: 6969 spans: platform Spans new.
    bridge subscribeStream: 'tel/log'.

    (* The runner says this boot is unproven. Everything below hangs off it. *)
    platform otaTrial
      ifTrue:  [ 'trial true' println ]
      ifFalse: [ 'trial FALSE — the env: header did not reach this test' println ].

    (* sha256 of 'abc' — a hash this node is certainly not already running, since
       no OEVM_IMAGE_HASH is set and `otaRunningHash` answers nil. *)
    rec:: platform Record tag: #App
            with: #image -> (platform Record tag: #BlobRef
                               with: #hash -> (platform ByteArray fromHex:
                                 'ba7816bf8f01cfea414140de5dae2223b00361a396177a9cb410ff61f20015ad')
                               with: #size -> 4096)
            with: #sig -> (platform ByteArray fromHex:
              'ab00ab00ab00ab00ab00ab00ab00ab00ab00ab00ab00ab00ab00ab00ab00ab00ab00ab00ab00ab00ab00ab00ab00ab00ab00ab00ab00ab00ab00ab00ab00ab00').

    (* The falsifier: this record IS one the bridge would act on. Assert it before
       asserting that the bridge does not. *)
    ('the record is stageable ' , ((bridge otaWantedFrom: rec) at: 1) byteSize printString) println.

    space put: 'goal/apps/main' value: rec.
    space drain.
    ('pending before ' , bridge pendingSize printString) println.

    (* The whole test. With the guard: returns immediately, writes nothing. Without
       it: `otaStage:` is called, fails, and logs `ota stage failed` — `pending
       after 1`. *)
    bridge otaCheck.
    space drain.
    ('pending after ' , bridge pendingSize printString) println.

    'still here — otaCheck returned and nothing exited' println.
  )
) : (
)
